  "body": "## Current Specification\r\n\r\nThe table at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/C/#dom-anchor says:\r\n\r\nFocusable area | DOM anchor\r\n----------------|-------------\r\nThe shapes of area elements in an image map .... | The img element\r\n\r\nA shape is a focusable area, instead of &lt;area>, and its DOM anchor is &lt;img>. `document.activeElement` should return the DOM anchor of the focused area, so if a shape is focused, the corresponding &lt;img> should be returned.\r\n\r\n## Reality\r\n\r\nWith Chrome, EdgeHTML, Firefox, Safari, `document.activeElement` is an &lt;area> if the shape defined by it is focused.\r\n\r\nShape's DOM anchor should be the &lt;area> defining it.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
